  Issues:
    - The on-Z mass window (86–96 GeV, width 10 GeV) is narrower than the typical CMS dilepton mass window for on-Z selections. CMS-SUS-16-034 specifies |m_ll − m_Z| < 15 GeV (i.e., 76.3–106.3 GeV). This tighter window would reduce signal acceptance.
    - Multiple Delphes runs were attempted and killed before the agent ran it in the background, wasting ~4 minutes of wall time.

